	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Felwood is a dying forest in the north of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}, between {link:ashenvale}Ashenvale{/link} to the south and the snows of {link:winterspring}Winterspring{/link} to the north-east. Its trees are black and twisted, its streams run green and foul, and its air smells of rot and smoke. Once it was the northern reach of the night elves' great forest. Now it is the wound the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link} left behind when it was driven from the world. The beasts of Felwood are mad, its furbolgs are savage, and demons still walk in its hollows. Yet a few druids remain in its southern glades, and they have not given up on it.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The forest was a home of the {link:night-elves}night elves{/link} for ages beyond count. Their moonwells and barrow dens lie scattered through it, and the white stones of the {link:ruins-of-constellas}Ruins of Constellas{/link} still stand in its western glades. The treant ancients who guarded the kaldorei made their homes among its trees. In the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, the Legion came to {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. The dreadlord {link:tichondrius}Tichondrius{/link} carried into the forest the Skull of {link:gul-dan}Gul'dan{/link}, a relic swollen with demonic power, and through it he poured corruption into the land. Infernals fell burning from the sky and left craters that fester still. When {link:illidan-stormrage}Illidan Stormrage{/link} took the power of the skull for himself and slew the dreadlord, the damage was already done. The forest that survived was a forest of the fel, and people began to call it Felwood.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[Felwood belongs to no one, and many powers contend for it. In the south, the druids of the {link:emerald-circle}Emerald Circle{/link} keep a small camp called the {link:emerald-sanctuary}Emerald Sanctuary{/link}, where they study the sickness and search for its cure. The {link:horde}Horde{/link} holds {link:bloodvenom-post}Bloodvenom Post{/link} in the west, and the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} keeps a hippogryph roost at {link:talonbranch-glade}Talonbranch Glade{/link} in the north-east. Between them lies the enemy. The warlocks of the {link:shadow-council}Shadow Council{/link} have made {link:jaedenar}Jaedenar{/link} the seat of their order, and there they bargain with demons. Jadefire {link:satyrs}satyrs{/link} foul the old moonwells. The {link:deadwood-furbolgs}Deadwood{/link} {link:furbolgs}furbolgs{/link} have gone mad. In the far north, the {link:timbermaw-furbolgs}Timbermaw{/link} furbolgs hold the pass to {link:winterspring}Winterspring{/link} and trust almost no one. The taint does not stay in Felwood: the druids of {link:darkshore}Darkshore{/link} fear it is seeping west into their own forests.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:emerald-circle}Emerald Circle{/link}.{/b} Druids of the {link:cenarion-circle}Cenarion Circle{/link}, of both the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} and the {link:horde}Horde{/link}, who have sworn to heal the forest.
• {b}The {link:shadow-council}Shadow Council{/link}.{/b} Warlocks and cultists who hold {link:jaedenar}Jaedenar{/link} with demons of the Legion at their side.
• {b}The Jadefire satyrs.{/b} They haunt the {link:ruins-of-constellas}Ruins of Constellas{/link}, {link:jadefire-glen}Jadefire Glen{/link} and {link:jadefire-run}Jadefire Run{/link}, and spread corruption wherever they go.
• {b}The {link:deadwood-furbolgs}Deadwood{/link} furbolgs.{/b} A tribe driven mad by the fel, with villages in the far south and far north of the forest.
• {b}The {link:timbermaw-furbolgs}Timbermaw{/link} furbolgs.{/b} The one tribe that has kept its mind, guarding the tunnels of {link:timbermaw-hold}Timbermaw Hold{/link}.
• {b}The corrupted wild.{/b} Warpwood elementals, blighted treants, oozes, maddened bears, wolves and owlbeasts, and infernals that still walk {link:shatter-scar-vale}Shatter Scar Vale{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Kaldorei Forest.{/b} For millennia the northern woods were a quiet land of moonwells, barrow dens and ancients.
• {b}The {link:third-war}Third War{/link}.{/b} The Legion's host marched on {link:mount-hyjal}Mount Hyjal{/link}. {link:tichondrius}Tichondrius{/link} corrupted the forest with the {link:skull-of-gul-dan}Skull of Gul'dan{/link}, and infernals were called down upon it.
• {b}{link:illidan-stormrage}Illidan{/link}'s Choice.{/b} Illidan Stormrage consumed the skull, took the shape of a demon and slew Tichondrius in these woods. His brother banished him for it.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} The Legion's host was broken at the {link:battle-of-mount-hyjal}Battle of Mount Hyjal{/link}, but Felwood did not heal. Demons, satyrs and warlocks remain, and only a handful of druids stand against them.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Forest",
			text = [=[• The druids of the {link:emerald-circle}Emerald Circle{/link} have learned to make a salve that returns a corrupted plant to health. Songflowers, windblossoms, whipper roots and night dragon blooms that were thought lost have flowered again under their care.
• A flute carved from the wood of a fallen ancient was found in the hands of a {link:satyrs}satyr{/link}. The ancient's spirit was bound inside it and could not rest until the waters of the {link:temple-of-the-moon}Temple of the Moon{/link} set it free.
• The {link:shadow-council}Shadow Council{/link} guards its fortress with four braziers whose names are Pain, Malice, Suffering and Hatred.
• The spirits of three ancients, {link:vartrus-the-ancient}Vartrus{/link}, Stoma and Hastat, still answer those who come to a certain rock in {link:irontree-woods}Irontree Woods{/link}.]=],
		},
	},
})

